              "text": "Here are a couple of options you can use, depending on where you are posting it (Slack, an email, or a farewell card).\n\n### Option 1: Fun, Inspiring, and Balanced (Great for Slack or Email)\n\n**To our resident Meme Lord and legendary Engineer, Stephen!** \ud83d\ude80\n\nIt\u2019s truly hard to imagine our codebase (and our Slack channels) without you. You didn't just solve some of our toughest engineering challenges with absolute brilliance; you did it while keeping the entire team laughing with your top-tier meme game. \n\nThank you for always raising the bar, debugging our systems, and debugging our bad days with the perfect GIF. \n\nAs you \"merge\" into this exciting next chapter, we know you\u2019re going to build incredible things. Our loss is your next team's massive win (and they have *no* idea how lucky they are to get your engineering genius and your legendary meme folder). \n\nWishing you nothing but success on your next adventure, Stephen. Keep compiling greatness, and never stop posting! \ud83d\udcbb\u2728\n\n***\n\n### Option 2: Short, Punchy, and Meme-Themed (Great for a Card)\n\n**Stephen, the man, the myth, the Meme-Engineering Legend!** \n\nThank you for being one of the absolute best engineers we\u2019ve ever had the privilege of working with. You came for the code, but you stayed for the memes\u2014and you made our team infinitely better because of both. \n\nWhile we are incredibly sad to see you go, we are so excited to see the amazing things you\u2019ll build next. Go crush it in your next chapter! \n\n*(We expect you to still drop by our channels occasionally just to drop a high-quality reaction GIF. Don't leave us on read!)* \n\nWishing you the absolute best!",
